{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196527-clear-sky-lightning-blue-jade-warstrider-artifact-\u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022","id":1196527,"title":"Clear Sky Lightning (Blue Jade Warstrider, Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-17T10:29:56-07:00","id":1196527,"title":"Clear Sky Lightning (Blue Jade Warstrider, Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Time of Tumult has brought new threats and, with them, the need for new weapons. Clear Sky Lightning is the Haslanti League\u2019s answer to the Bull of the North and his Icewalkers \u2013 or will be, the artificer Chevin Snow-Crowned tells the Admiralty, if they give him his pick of the jade and sorcerous artifacts recovered from the old empire\u2019s ruins. The young Dragon-blooded\u2019s words carry weight in Haslanti councils, but a hundred other voices clamor for those same resources. For now, the warstrider is only half-complete, a feathersteel body waiting for a blue jade soul.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attunement:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 15m</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soak:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 15; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hardness:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 10</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Damage track:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> -0x5/-1x5/-2x10/-4x10</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed Bonus:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> +3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hearthstone slot(s):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Era:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Time of Tumult</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Standard Armaments</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crossbow: Close ACC \u22121; Short +5; Medium +3; Long +1; +16L DMG, OVW 4, Crossbow, Piercing, Powerful</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sledgehammer: +1 ACC, +14L DMG, +0 DEF, OVW 5, Reaching, Smashing, Two-Handed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unarmed: +5 ACC, +10B DMG, +0 DEF, OVW 3, Grappling, Natural, Smashing</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Evocations of Clear Sky Lightning</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clear-Sky Lightning\u2019s feathersteel frame is lighter than most warstriders\u2019. When attuned, it can stand on any surface strong enough to support a yeddim, and the pilot receives a two-mote discount on Charms such as Graceful Crane Stance that would further lighten it. Once per turn, its mechanisms can reflexively reload its crossbow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Heavens-Dispatched Bolt</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Resonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lightning does not fear its fall to earth. This Evocation supplements a movement action to jump from an elevated position. Clear Sky Lightning falls at two range bands per turn and does not take falling damage. If used at the start of combat, the fall completes immediately (don\u2019t track multiple turns of falling from an arbitrary height in combat time).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant: If used at the start of combat, the pilot can act a number of ticks earlier equal to the number of range bands fallen, to a maximum of four.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Thunder Follows Lightning</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Dissonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Heavens-Dispatched Bolt</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clear Sky Lightning strikes the ground with tremendous force, scattering all before it. This Evocation may be used at the end of a fall and applies an environmental hazard within as many range bands as were fallen (to a maximum of medium range). The hazard affects all characters \u2013 including allies \u2013 within range, and has a difficulty of (pilot\u2019s Essence + 1) and damage 4B. Characters that take damage from the hazard fall prone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Waive the mote cost of this Evocation if it is used at the end of a jump enhanced with Heavens-Dispatched Bolt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dissonant: As long as the pilot isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, she may invoke this Evocation reflexively as her devastating action (Arms, p. 141).</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Voltaic Lodestone Binding</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m+; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Resonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until the grapple ends</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hair-raising potential runs through Clear Sky Lightning\u2019s sledgehammer, turning it into an enormous lodestone. This Evocation creates a (Strength + Melee) grapple gambit with the sledgehammer against a smaller enemy wearing or carrying metal armor or weapons. If the gambit succeeds, the target is magnetically attached to the hammer, and the warstrider and its pilot gain the following benefits:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They ignore the -2 Defense penalty from grappling.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The pilot may take combat actions as normal.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If she makes a withering or decisive attack against another target with the sledgehammer, this is also treated as a savage action against the grappled victim. In the withering case, damage is determined based on the attack roll\u2019s successes only (ignore the weapon\u2019s base damage). In the decisive case, up to (Warstrider Strength) dice of damage may be applied against the victim instead of the attack\u2019s target, ignoring Hardness.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The gambit may also be applied to battle groups by spending an additional (Size) motes. Affected characters can end the grapple immediately if they can wriggle out of their metal armor or release their metal weapons, but may suffer damage from the resulting fall. The armor and weapons remain attached to the sledgehammer for the duration of the grapple.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant: If the pilot knows Thunder Follows Lightning, that Evocation is permanently enhanced. It now also affects airborne characters within range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Crackling Snare</span></span></b><br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Voltaic Lodestone Binding, Elemental Bolt Attack<br /> <br /> This Evocation upgrades its prerequisites. The Dragon-Blood may activate them both at the same time, creating a (Dexterity + [Archery or Thrown]) grapple gambit with the Air-aspected elemental bolt out to its range and subject to the same conditions as Voltaic Lodestone Binding. If the gambit succeeds, the target is pulled onto the sledgehammer and all the other effects of Voltaic Lodestone Binding Apply.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Wind-Light Ascent</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Dissonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Panels on the back of Clear Sky Lightning unfold, exposing the two cylinders of blue jade that form its core. The warstrider propels itself on jets of wind and light. This Evocation supplements a movement action, increasing the warstrider\u2019s Speed bonus to +5 and allowing it to jump up one range band as part of its movement. If the pilot knows Thunder Follows Lightning, she may activate it at the end of this movement.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dissonant: As long as the pilot isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, she may use this Evocation to reflexively jump if the surface she is standing on collapses or is destroyed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Storm-Wing Rider</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: \u2014; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Resonant, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Heavens-Dispatched Bolt, Wind-Light Ascent</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When mastered, Clear Sky Lightning severs all attachment to the earth for a time. When she uses its prerequisite, the pilot may activate this Evocation to grant her warstrider true flight. Each turn, she may move one range band in any direction, or choose to hover in place. To maintain this, she must pay one Initiative per turn, and it immediately ends if she enters Initiative Crash. At any time during the flight she may activate Heavens-Dispatched Bolt to immediately return to earth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Outside of combat, this Evocation grants about fifteen minutes of flight before Clear Sky Lightning needs to land to recharge for an hour. Its long-distance flight speed is the same as its overland speed (Arms, p. 142).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resonant: The pilot does not need to pay Initiative to maintain this Evocation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Lightning Battery Discharge</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Dual, Dissonant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Any three Evocations</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infused with the essence of sky and storm, Clear Sky Lightning\u2019s crossbow can become something more. This Evocation is identical to Lightning Ballista Fusillade (Arms, p. 150), except that even a pilot resonant with jade cannot use it as her devastating action (Arms, p. 141).</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Head-in-Clouds Approach</span></span></b><br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Elemental Succor Method<br /> <br /> This Evocation upgrades Elemental Concentration Trance (WFHW, p. XX), Elemental Empowerment Meditation (WFHW, p. XX), and Elemental Succor Method (WFHW, p. XX). The Dragon-Blood gains the following benefits:<ul><li>When she uses Elemental Concentration Trance, Clear Sky Lightning itself counts as an expression of the element of Air.</li> <li>When she uses Elemental Empowerment Meditation, she may also use the motes gained on Evocations of Clear Sky Lightning.</li> <li>When she uses Elemental Succor Method, she may use it to instead repair one of Clear Sky Lightning\u2019s -1 or -2 health levels.</li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Sky-Crossing Thunderbolt</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Storm-Wing Rider</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clear Sky Lightning returns to its source, disappearing in a bolt of lighting that ascends to the heavens. Moments later, it falls once more. Once per story, the pilot may use this Evocation to teleport the warstrider to any location within (Essence) miles that is open to the sky. She may activate Heavens-Dispatched Bolt for free, and this counts as a fall from maximum distance for its purposes and for Thunder Follows Lightning.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Twilight Caste Solar who knows this Evocation can extend her anima ability (Exalted, p. 176) to Clear Sky Lightning.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">The Shrike Itself</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: \u2014; Mins: Essence 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Sky-Crossing Thunderbolt, God-King\u2019s Shrike</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To the enlightened sage, Clear Sky Lightning\u2019s blue jade core reflects the sky itself and all beneath it. The Solar may activate this Evocation when she uses God-King\u2019s Shrike (Exalted, p. 340). She may invest the committed motes into the warstrider, and use them to pay the cost of its Evocations during the calamity \u2013 if she is present for it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note: I plan to add a couple of Evocations that upgrade Dragon-blooded Charms once What Fire Has Wrought is released.</span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TZX8W6HWUHcW1WEjZzbLy_31VPpYBHu9cCcpfKNwgEs/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Google Docs link</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 04-20-2018, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:43:32-07:00","id":1196659,"title":"","content":"Three words: PREPARE FOR TITANFALL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:03:41-07:00","id":1209415,"title":"","content":"Updated with a couple of charm-upgrade evocations for Dragon-blooded based on the WFHW preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}